WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.475
This is Inside Politics

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:09.142
with Bernard

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.478
Shaw and Judy Woodruff in Washington.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.347
That was June 7th.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.683
1993 Judy Woodruff's

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.984
first day in the anchor

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.419
chair of Inside Politics.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.954
She along with our late

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:22.389
former colleague Bernard Shaw,

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.758
made Inside Politics must see TV

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:25.392
for knowing

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:26.559
what is happening

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.695
on the campaign trail and beyond.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.362
And guess what?

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.231
I'm honored to have Judy here with me

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.466
today on my first day in this

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.034
in this chair.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.169
Judy, of course, works for the PBS

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.537
NewsHour now.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.605
So good to have you here.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.340
And I am so happy to be here.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:40.907
I'm having

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.542
kind of an out of body experience

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:42.876
right now.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:43.943
I have to be honest.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.812
All these memories come flooding back

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.213
many memories.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.081
What did you learn

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.649
covering politics on the show

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.850
for so long?

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.585
I think the thing that I learned

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:52.919
and of course,

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.621
it was a very different era. Oh, yeah.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.321
We were just saying that

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.523
was 30 years ago.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.360
Was it politics can be civil,

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.163
that it matters a lot

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.365
and that it affects every person

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.533
in this country.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:09.202
It's not something that's just we

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.236
we spent a lot of time

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:11.137
talking about

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.206
what personalities are up to

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.841
and who said what about whom.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.642
But in the end,

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.410
it affects the American people.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.479
And I think for me, that was the

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.914
that was the biggest takeaway.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:21.147
Okay.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:22.715
Well, let's actually show our viewers

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.983
some of the flavor

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.085
of what you're talking about.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.553
I want to take you on a trip down

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.421
memory lane, Judy Woodruff

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.891
from some of your shows in the nineties

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.927
It's the name that has spent more money

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.995
than anyone has spent in Iowa

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.597
in a Republican caucus race.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.832
At the 1980 convention,

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:39.499
I was working for

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.868
another television network at that time

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.970
and it was such a great story

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:44.671
to be working on

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.306
whether Ronald Reagan was going to pick

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.141
former President Gerald Ford.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.176
If you add up what he got

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.244
in terms of a vote

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.412
and what you got

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.380
and he asked you to get out of the race,

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.782
he might have been the winner.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.650
What would you say to Bob Dole?

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.053
There may not be a war room per se,

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:00.720
but White House

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.355
officials certainly seem in

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.723
full battle mode

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:05.658
now.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.260
The hairstyles, which

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.395
were awesome, I'd say

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.664
they were very open up here and very I'm

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.666
glad you're always on trend.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.835
But it did it did feel different.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.704
Are you optimistic

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.772
that American can get even

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.374
maybe not back to that,

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.042
but closer to that?

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.010
Oh, I am.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.744
I mean,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:25.345
as I think

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.813
I suggested a minute ago, Dana,

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.381
we are in a very

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.850
we're in a tough moment right now.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.385
In American politics.

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:32.919
There's just

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.854
a lot of mudslinging happening

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.056
and people are angry.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.324
But, in fact,

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.058
you know, people

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.493
the two political parties

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.361
were at each other's throats

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.163
and but it was just much more civil.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:46.432
I mean, I remember covering

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.067
Bob Dole

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.969
and then Harry Reid

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.304
going at each other than Harry.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.039
Harry Reid called

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:53.907
President George

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.642
W Bush a loser

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.877
and then apologized for it.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.913
It was it was just a different

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.714
a different tone at the time.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:01.981
Yeah.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.550
I was thinking you're saying Bob Dole

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.083
I was is

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.485
stop lying about my record

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.754
when he said that to George H.W.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.821
Bush. Right.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.890
And it was a huge deal it was.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.392
But there were actually

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.160
politicians apologizing

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.495
about what they had said.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:16.863
So we learned a lot

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.631
and we covered big stories.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.700
We covered everything from

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.202
nine 11, which, of course,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.604
you know, consume what we

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.838
were doing at this network

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.941
for four months.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.876
The Gingrich revolution

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.077
you remember that in 19

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:32.245
we thought that was as crazy

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.246
as it was going to get.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:34.714
I want to ask you, if I may.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.150
You're working on a project now at PBS

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.651
where you're going out

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.019
and talking to voters

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.389
and trying to find out if America can get

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.558
across that divide.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.627
And I'm finding that it's a work

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:48.661
in progress.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.162
You're right.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.964
I'm spending these next two years

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.599
with the News Hour PBS,

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.733
traveling around the country,

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.868
interviewing voters and experts about

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.470
why we're so divided.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.805
Where did that come from?

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.607
And I'm finding it's remarkable

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:00.974
in a place

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:01.841
like Oklahoma,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.875
where 100 years ago

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.978
they had a terrible race massacre.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.213
They're still having debates over

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.415
how to teach the history of race

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.183
in the schools.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:11.050
It's it's

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.353
a it's a great education and it's a

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.188
it's a work in progress.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:16.623
I'm always optimistic.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.825
Dan, I know you you know that

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.493
But but and at this point,

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.961
I have confidence

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.229
that the American people, Judy,

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:23.830
are going to do the right.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.732
It is really such an honor

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:26.366
that you're here.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:27.133
Thank you for taking

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:27.734
so proud

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:28.835
to return

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.537
Back to CNN desk assistant to anchor.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:32.672
So proud of you.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.206
Thank you.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:33.806
Thanks, Judy.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.441
And I also want to remember

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.243
Bernard Shaw, who passed away

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:38.111
nine months ago.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.879
He was a journalist, journalist.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:42.215
He led the way in being a good person,

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.416
both on and off the air.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.485
We're really we really do miss him.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.786
I also want to thank John King

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.388
for reviving the story

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.389
Inside Politics

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.857
brand about a decade ago,

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.659
building it back to a show

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.193
where viewers can get information

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.995
from the best in the business.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.797
Thanks for joining Inside Politics.

